From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: uniform bind trims, one GPU-modified walk and one bank set insert (EDEN_UP_UBO_BIND_TRIM)

DRAFT, not built. Our own work (no upstream port). Gated by EDEN_UP_UBO_BIND_TRIM (exact 1), a
live switch (Id UboBindTrim, not armed); off by default, needs nothing at boot. On: a uniform
bind reuses its first GPU-modified walk for use_fast_buffer unless a tracker-changing block ran
in between, and skips native_indirect_uniforms_this_frame.insert for a bank its per-slot memo
stamped this frame. EDEN_UP_UBO_BIND_TRIM_VERIFY=1 (boot, BufferCache constructor) makes both
anyway and compares. 10 s line while on: "EDEN_UP_UBO_BIND_TRIM: X s, N draws; ...".

Reviewed draft from the draws job, v2: reviewer decided the plain reuse case inline in the &&
chain instead of an out-of-line call, and replaced the one-frame "skip size now" field with
"skip size 0 in N of M frames (now X)" (two new counters); gain estimate lowered to about
+0.05-0.15 fps in the review.
---
